commit 49b1904191ed3ed6a19aec39907d60d380245e14
Author: Prasad Shirvalkar <prasad.shirvalkar@ucsf.edu>
Date:   Sat Jun 27 04:17:40 2026 -0700

    CS-4 wiring: surface per-PRO LSB selection on the timeline (backend + frontend)
    
    The staged per_pro_lsb API now drives the timeline — each pain rating gets one
    LSB value chosen by the CS-4 source precedence, tagged with its tier.
    
    Backend (bravo_service):
    - _pro_lsb_by_channel: for each channel with a resolvable sensing center, run
      availability.per_pro_lsb over the PRO timestamps (pain['t']) with the SAME
      inputs lsb_series uses — that channel's native series, TD-bearing recordings
      (streaming td_list + montage/survey psd_list, all 250 Hz TD) for tier 2, and
      the CS-3 PSD-only event blocks for tier 3. Center = configured sensing center
      (canonical key), falling back to the series' own first finite center_hz.
    - _build_availability emits pro_lsb in the payload (and {} in the error path);
      keyed by raw channel -> [{t,lsb,tier,center_hz,used_s,saturated,reason}].
    - Fixed an array truth-value guard (pro_times arrives as an ndarray).
    
    Frontend (BiomarkerDataTimeline):
    - proLsbFor(ch): collapse raw keys onto the lane, keep ratings that resolved
      (tier != null).
    - Per-rating overlay on each LSB lane: one point per rating at its selected LSB,
      SHAPE = source tier (native filled circle / TD-transform open circle /
      PSD-bridge open diamond), red outline = TD window saturated. binMode colors by
      pain bin; otherwise a steel tone (shape carries the tier). Hover names the
      tier, LSB, Hz, and bin.
    - Glyph-legend entry + PAL.proLsb; nLegRows 7->8 (non-bin mode).
    
    Verified live on RCS08: 684 PROs x 30 channels -> 239 per-rating LSB values
    (51 native, 102 TD-transform, 86 PSD-bridge), the precedence in action; the rest
    honestly None (no coincident recording on that channel). Tests +1
    (test_wiring_pro_lsb_by_channel_builds_per_channel_series). Suite 232/232.

